{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "note": "The formula family (2026-11-10): the look of F45 Jurong West's own running ads, as a second family beside the reference set. The area callout across the top, the duration and the offer low in the frame, plain filled type with a soft shadow and no outline, colour pairings chosen to sit on a plain backdrop, no logo and no brand colour. A batch uses one family (brief.look, else creative_defaults.look): 'reference' is offer-treatments / offer-styles / offer-palettes, 'formula' is this file. Same schema as those files; every entry carries family 'formula'. Both groups float clear of faces (float: { edge?, min_h_pct, gap_pct }): the lower block starts below the lowest face under it if at least min_h_pct of the canvas is left, else it moves above the heads; the callout (edge 'top') is cut short above a face. The lower block's scrim is 'local': full strength behind the block, fading above and below, so a plain backdrop is never tinted to the frame's edge. No contrast stroke: a line that a scrim cannot rescue gets a band. Contrast is judged at the large-text level (3:1): every line is display type, 40 px or more.",
